{
  "about": "Layers.hitStack on both phones: the page's elements back to front, and what a fingertip touchRadius round at each probe lands on, top-most first. A hidden element is never listed; a group is one row, \"group:<id>\", listed where its top-most touched member is, with its shown members (a group left with one shown member is that member's row); a member of a cropped group is touched only where the crop shows it; anything thinner than twice the radius is touched as if grown to that about its centre, a turned one in its turned frame. Probes stay clear of edges, so the iPhone's 4-unit slack does not matter. A probe's own touchRadius overrides the top-level one. behind gives Alt+Tab's next row for a selection: the row under the one holding it, round to the top past the bottom, the top when none holds it, null when there is no other row. oneRow says whether a selection is one whole row of the page's Layers list (one loose element, or every member of one outermost group, hidden ones too): Alt+Tab and Select what is behind step only from such a selection, and are refused otherwise. lid is a locked element (a backdrop to a hold) lying over the shape under: a hold on it lists both under Select behind. behindPoint gives where Alt+Tab and Select what is behind look (at): the last tap, when anything selected lies under it there, else the middle of the selection's box (null with nothing selected); steps says whether they step from there (the selection is one row and two or more rows lie at that point). g-far is a group at opposite sides of the page, its box middle over the backdrop alone, a photo under far-a only: with no tap on it, Alt+Tab is refused.",
